407 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T ( The Streamlit app re-runs the entire script from beginning to end every time the user interacts with the widget \(e.g. clicking a button, entering text\).  This is what makes Streamlit simple, but it introduces a problem: every time the script is re-run, all previous variable values are lost. Bad example: Creating a counter with a regular variable)
/E ( The Streamlit app re-runs the entire script from beginning to end every time the user interacts with the widget \(e.g. clicking a button, entering text\).  This is what makes Streamlit simple, but it introduces a problem: every time the script is re-run, all previous variable values are lost. Bad example: Creating a counter with a regular variable)
/Alt ()
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6 7]
>>
endobj
